    contentHtml: "<p>I’ve done 14 Full IronMan Races…. Almost 16 but I DNF two (did not finish).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trained myself on all of them with a goal to just finish.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>After I DNF in FLA last year, I got a little nervous that I wasn’t putting in the training I needed to complete my ultimate goal of not just crossing the finish line at the World Championship IronMan Race in Kona, but finishing this race strong.&nbsp;&nbsp;I decided to hire a coach!&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>After doing some research, I decided to hire Wendy Mader as my coach…. Boy, she did not know what she was getting into when she said “yes.”&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>She has been amazing…. Challenging me, questioning my “WHY” on certain training days….&nbsp;&nbsp;I love it.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>I hired Wendy in May, but we had never met… not until today..&nbsp;&nbsp;life was just too busy…&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>But God….&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>I was getting my bike looked at and she walks in and says… “ hey, I know you.”&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Gotta love social media..&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Anyway.. if you need a coach for your next IronMan Adventure… I highly recommend this amazing Kona World Champion Coach!&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;She is amazing&nbsp;</p>",
