    readTime: "1 min read",
    cover: "",
    excerpt: "Wendy has been my triathlon coach since 2010 when I decided to do my first Ironman. I had previously met her and attended a triathlon camp that she led. I liked her...",
    sourceUrl: "https://t2coaching.com/karen-kona-qualifier/",
    contentHtml: "<p>Wendy has been my triathlon coach since 2010 when I decided to do my first Ironman. I had previously<br />met her and attended a triathlon camp that she led. I liked her coaching style, expertise and experience.<br />I had been doing shorter triathlons for quite a few years, so the Ironman distance was daunting for me.<br />Wendy put together a training plan for me that was challenging, but attainable. I felt great doing that<br />first Ironman and have since completed nine Ironman events and just recently qualified for the Kona<br />World Championship and was rated fifth in the World in the Ironman rankings.</p>\n\n<p><br />One of the most beneficial things about working with Wendy is that she review my workouts and<br />comments about them. She adjusts future workouts based on my fatigue, where I am in my fitness level<br />and if I have personal obligations. She is responsive to my questions and changes in schedule. She<br />always accommodates any races or events that I want to do even though they may not be ideal to the<br />training plan.</p>\n\n<p><br />I have come so far in training with Wendy. I started with sprints, Olympics, half Ironmans, and then<br />some full Ironmans. I have qualified and participated in several 70.3 World Championships and<br />Nationals. I have been on the podium for a lot of them and I credit Wendy’s coaching to getting me<br />there.</p>",
